    "b-10-work-record-the-implementation-added-11": {
      "id": "b-10-work-record-the-implementation-added-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The implementation added streamed unlimited-size archive files, all typed source fields, source and media versions, dictionary/export evidence, stable IDs, explicit null dates, a rebuildable local index, and a loopback Data viewer. The native app gained Data navigation. Finished server records gained raw.txt and clean.txt artifacts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-work-record-a-staged-migration-copie-12": {
      "id": "b-10-work-record-a-staged-migration-copie-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A staged migration copied WisprSync, then live SQLite and the September 15 backup. Independent verification compared every field, all metadata objects from the export, and large-media hashes. Duplicate descriptors were normalized without deleting files. The verified archive moved to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/Users/Ford/Transcripts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-work-record-six-archive-tests-fourt-13": {
      "id": "b-10-work-record-six-archive-tests-fourt-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Six archive tests, fourteen server tests, app/server builds, and two isolated real-audio-to-archive tests passed. The previous installed app and server were kept in "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".local/install-backups",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Both production engines became ready after a second server restart. The Data page was verified with real archive counts and raw/clean details; synthetic records stayed outside production data."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
